      "content": "Acknowledge the 5% difference is real but explain it signifies a \"false positive rate\" where older demographics are more sensitive to a specific initial adjustment that the competitor's dosing algorithm avoids. Instead of hiding the data, suggest framing this 5% as a high-risk, low-benefit group that is easily weaned off the drug, thereby protecting 95% of the target market from unnecessary exposure. The rep should confidently clarify that while the competitor avoids this specific acute reaction, it does so at the cost of a 15% lower long-term efficacy in the same patient population.",
